Technical Specification: Intercom Smart Adapter & Receiver (ESP32-C3)This document provides a detailed overview, electrical schematics, and structural logic for the in-unit Intercom Smart Adapter. Designed to fit inside a standard analog handset (e.g., Urmet CS1132), this module intercepts high-voltage ringing signals, implements time-based automatic gate opening, and plays custom RTTTL melodies.1. Core Concepts & Safety IsolationThe analog coordinate lines of multi-family buildings are sensitive. Bridging digital microcontrollers directly onto the bus presents serious risks:Over-voltage: Call lines carry high voltages ($12\text{V AC} - 24\text{V DC}$) containing switching spikes that easily destroy $3.3\text{V}$ logic gates.Line Interference (Off-hook bug): Drawing continuous power from the microphone/audio lines drops the bus impedance, locking the entire building's riser into a permanent "handset lifted" state.1.1. Galvanic Isolation (Optocoupler Guard)We route the incoming ringing wire away from the handset's internal terminal CA and feed it exclusively into a PC817 Optocoupler. This physical light barrier prevents feedback loops, ensuring that the neighbor's handsets and the main control unit are electrically isolated from our microcontroller.2. Principle Electrical Schematic (Adapter Module)  ANALOG INTERCOM INPUT (Call line AC Rectification & Filtering)
